@lang en
IMPORT `vn14-ch5-claims-and-termination`

-- The hostile reading: each assertion below states the SURPRISING answer the document gives,
-- as encoded, and passes. A passing assertion here is evidence of a defect in the instrument,
-- not of a defect in the encoding. NOTES.md section 4 carries each finding with its source
-- lines and its scenario; the numbers X1 ... X26 are the same. Findings marked "reading only"
-- in NOTES.md have no assertion here.

§ `Findings`

§§ `Shared fixtures`

`the usual accounts` MEANS
    `The accounts` WITH
        `the Policyholder's account value`   IS 60_000_000
        `the Insured Member's account value` IS 40_000_000
        `the vesting ratio`                  IS 30%

GIVEN `as at` IS A DATE
      `born` IS A DATE
      `in Vietnam` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The person's particulars`
`a long-serving member, as at` `as at` `, born` `born` `, in Vietnam` `in Vietnam` MEANS
    `The person's particulars` WITH
        `as at`                                          IS `as at`
        `date of birth`                                  IS `born`
        `recorded in the List of Insured Members`        IS TRUE
        `present in Vietnam`                             IS `in Vietnam`
        `holds a valid Enrolment Form`                   IS TRUE
        `premium for this person paid to the Company`    IS TRUE
        `resident in Vietnam`                            IS TRUE
        `of full civil capacity under the Civil Code`    IS TRUE
        `full years of employment with the Policyholder` IS JUST 20

GIVEN `state` IS A `A state of the part`
      `account value` IS A NUMBER
      `crime by the Policyholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A death claim`
`an adult's death claim, part` `state` `, account value` `account value` `, crime by the Policyholder` `crime by the Policyholder` MEANS
    `A death claim` WITH
        `date of birth of the Insured Member`              IS YMD 1980 1 1
        `date of death`                                    IS YMD 2026 5 1
        `date of the event causing death`                  IS YMD 2026 5 1
        `date the Company received the death claim`        IS YMD 2026 5 10
        `the Contract was in force at death`               IS TRUE
        `state of the part at death`                       IS `state`
        `sum insured at the time of death`                 IS 1_000_000_000
        `account value on the date the claim was received` IS `account value`
        `premium paid after the date of the death claim`   IS 0
        `funeral benefit already paid`                     IS 0
        `benefits arising after death already paid`       IS 0
        `debt`                                             IS 0
        `reasonable costs incurred by the Company`         IS 0
        `suicide or a suicidal act, sane or insane`        IS FALSE
        `a criminal act of the Insured Member`             IS FALSE
        `a criminal act of the Policyholder`               IS `crime by the Policyholder`
        `a criminal act of a Beneficiary`                  IS FALSE

`a Basic Plan part in force since 2020` MEANS
    `An Insured Member's part` WITH
        `coverage start date`                    IS YMD 2020 1 1
        `maturity date`                          IS YMD 2040 1 1
        `latest reinstatement date`              IS NOTHING
        `plan`                                   IS `the Basic Plan`
        `sum insured`                            IS 1_000_000_000
        `sum insured at the coverage start date` IS 1_000_000_000
        `accounts`                               IS `the usual accounts`
        `debt`                                   IS 0
        `state`                                  IS `in force`

§§ `X1 — 28.4 and 11.2 read with 1.4: a birthday, or a business trip, ends the cover`

-- A member covered at 50 to a Maturity Date at 70 (the certificate's), aged 66 on 2 March 2026:
-- under the continuing reading (fork F24) the part "ends immediately" under 28.4. A member of
-- 40 on a business trip abroad on the day the test is made: the same.
#ASSERT `28.4 — the Insured Member, on these particulars, no longer meets Article 1.4` (`a long-serving member, as at` (YMD 2026 3 2) `, born` (YMD 1960 3 1) `, in Vietnam` TRUE)
#ASSERT `28.4 — the Insured Member, on these particulars, no longer meets Article 1.4` (`a long-serving member, as at` (YMD 2026 3 2) `, born` (YMD 1986 3 1) `, in Vietnam` FALSE)
#ASSERT `28 — the part ends on` `the Insured Member no longer meets Article 1.4 or the agreed conditions`

§§ `X2 — Temporary cover: a covered accident can pay less than an excluded suicide`

GIVEN `suicide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A death during temporary cover`
`a temporary-cover death on 150,000,000 of premium and 100,000,000 pending sum insured, suicide` `suicide` MEANS
    `A death during temporary cover` WITH
        `cover applied for under the main product`                                 IS TRUE
        `date the Company stamped receipt of the complete valid application`      IS YMD 2026 3 1
        `date the Company received the full first premium`                         IS YMD 2026 3 1
        `date the temporary cover period ended`                                    IS NOTHING
        `date of death`                                                            IS YMD 2026 3 20
        `date of the event that led to death`                                      IS YMD 2026 3 20
        `an event or continuous chain of events, objective in nature`              IS TRUE
        `caused by a sudden external force or object acting on the body`           IS TRUE
        `the direct and sole cause of death, unrelated to any other cause`         IS TRUE
        `suicide, whether sane or insane`                                          IS `suicide`
        `a criminal act of the Insured Member, the Policyholder or a Beneficiary`  IS FALSE
        `would be accepted at the standard rate on the declared information`       IS TRUE
        `total sum insured of the main product on all pending applications for this person` IS 100_000_000
        `total premium paid on all pending applications`                           IS 150_000_000
        `medical and underwriting costs the Company paid`                          IS 2_000_000

-- The accident: the lesser of 100,000,000 and 200,000,000, "and the premium paid is not
-- refunded" -- 100,000,000. The suicide: 150,000,000 less 2,000,000 costs = 148,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the outcome of a death during temporary cover` (`a temporary-cover death on 150,000,000 of premium and 100,000,000 pending sum insured, suicide` FALSE) EQUALS `the temporary benefit, with no refund of premium, of` 100_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the outcome of a death during temporary cover` (`a temporary-cover death on 150,000,000 of premium and 100,000,000 pending sum insured, suicide` TRUE) EQUALS `a refund of the premium paid, without interest, of` 148_000_000

§§ `X4 — Temporary cover for a member added after the Contract was issued`

-- 11.1 adds a member in 2027 to a Contract issued 1 January 2026. Article 3's period begins at
-- the stamp (10 January 2027) and "ends on the Contract Issue Date" (1 January 2026): it never
-- holds a single day.
`a member added in 2027 to a Contract issued in 2026` MEANS
    `A death during temporary cover` WITH
        `cover applied for under the main product`                                 IS TRUE
        `date the Company stamped receipt of the complete valid application`      IS YMD 2027 1 10
        `date the Company received the full first premium`                         IS YMD 2027 1 10
        `date the temporary cover period ended`                                    IS JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)
        `date of death`                                                            IS YMD 2027 1 20
        `date of the event that led to death`                                      IS YMD 2027 1 20
        `an event or continuous chain of events, objective in nature`              IS TRUE
        `caused by a sudden external force or object acting on the body`           IS TRUE
        `the direct and sole cause of death, unrelated to any other cause`         IS TRUE
        `suicide, whether sane or insane`                                          IS FALSE
        `a criminal act of the Insured Member, the Policyholder or a Beneficiary`  IS FALSE
        `would be accepted at the standard rate on the declared information`       IS TRUE
        `total sum insured of the main product on all pending applications for this person` IS 100_000_000
        `total premium paid on all pending applications`                           IS 5_000_000
        `medical and underwriting costs the Company paid`                          IS 0

#ASSERT NOT `3.1 — under` `a member added in 2027 to a Contract issued in 2026` `, the temporary cover period includes` (YMD 2027 1 10)
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the outcome of a death during temporary cover` `a member added in 2027 to a Contract issued in 2026` EQUALS `no temporary benefit is payable`

§§ `X5 — Article 5 provides for two breaches and no others`

GIVEN `deliberate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would have declined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would have charged more` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A breach of the duty to declare`
`a material breach:` `deliberate` `,` `would have declined` `,` `would have charged more` MEANS
    `A breach of the duty to declare` WITH
        `deliberate`                                                            IS `deliberate`
        `the Company would not have accepted the risk had it known`             IS `would have declined`
        `the Company would have accepted only at a higher premium had it known` IS `would have charged more`
        `it affected the decision to accept or to reinstate`                    IS TRUE
        `an inaccurate or omitted declaration of age or gender only`            IS FALSE

`a 5.2 refund` MEANS
    `A refund under Article 5.2` WITH
        `accounts`              IS `the usual accounts`
        `termination charge`    IS 0
        `debt`                  IS 0
        `benefits already paid` IS 0

-- An honest mistake the Company would have declined; a deliberate one it would only have rated.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 5 — the consequence of` (`a material breach:` FALSE `,` TRUE `,` FALSE) `, with a refund computed from` `a 5.2 refund`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 5 — the consequence of` (`a material breach:` TRUE `,` FALSE `,` TRUE) `, with a refund computed from` `a 5.2 refund`

§§ `X6 — 6.2 takes the withdrawals off twice`

-- The member withdrew 10,000,000; the Account Value is 100,000,000 AFTER that withdrawal; the
-- premium paid is 80,000,000. 6.2 refunds the greater (100,000,000) "less withdrawals": 90,000,000,
-- one withdrawal counted twice. (No Debt, no costs, no benefits paid.)
`a member found to be over 65 at entry` MEANS
    `The money in a part at the Company's notice` WITH
        `date of birth as declared`                           IS YMD 1970 1 1
        `true date of birth`                                  IS YMD 1955 1 1
        `coverage start date`                                 IS YMD 2024 1 15
        `account value at the Company's notice`               IS 100_000_000
        `premium paid for the part`                           IS 80_000_000
        `premium paid by the Insured Member`                  IS 20_000_000
        `premium paid by the Policyholder`                    IS 60_000_000
        `benefits paid`                                       IS 0
        `withdrawals from the Insured Member's account value` IS 10_000_000
        `debt`                                                IS 0
        `reasonable underwriting costs`                       IS 0
        `accounts`                                            IS `the usual accounts`

#ASSERT NOT `6.1 — the true Age is within the insurable ages` `a member found to be over 65 at entry`
#ASSERT `6.2 — the refund` `a member found to be over 65 at entry` EQUALS 90_000_000

§§ `X7 — A death during account suspension pays nothing, not even the member's own account`

#ASSERT `Chapter 2 — the outcome of the death claim, for` `a Basic Plan part in force since 2020` `and` (`an adult's death claim, part` `suspended` `, account value` 100_000_000 `, crime by the Policyholder` FALSE) EQUALS `no benefit: the part was suspended under Article 20`
#ASSERT NOT `20.2 — the death benefit is performed while suspended`

§§ `X8 — 16.2.1 and 16.2.3 send the same payment to different places`

-- 25,000,000 paid on 20 June for a 30 June due date, nothing overdue, rider premium designated.
-- 16.2.1: every Periodic Premium due is paid (there is none), so all of it is Top-up Premium.
-- 16.2.3: it goes first to the NEXT instalment.
`an early payment with nothing overdue` MEANS
    `A premium payment` WITH
        `amount`                                                    IS 25_000_000
        `date paid`                                                 IS YMD 2026 6 20
        `Premium Due Date`                                          IS YMD 2026 6 30
        `insurance year`                                            IS 2
        `the Policyholder has designated payment of rider premiums` IS TRUE
        `all basic premium instalments due have been paid`          IS TRUE
        `instalment`                                                IS 10_000_000
        `instalments due and unpaid`                                IS 0
        `the Policyholder directed otherwise`                       IS FALSE

#ASSERT (`16.2.1 — the allocation of` `an early payment with nothing overdue`)'s `top-up premium` EQUALS 25_000_000
#ASSERT `16.2.2 and 16.2.3 — the order of application of` `an early payment with nothing overdue` EQUALS LIST `the instalments due and unpaid`, `the next instalment`, `the Top-up Premium`

§§ `X9 — Article 15: the Policyholder's crime, and no payee`

-- The employer (the Policyholder) commits a crime directly related to the employee's death:
-- the employee's Beneficiaries lose the death benefit.
#ASSERT `15 — the death is excluded, for` `a Basic Plan part in force since 2020` `and` (`an adult's death claim, part` `in force` `, account value` 100_000_000 `, crime by the Policyholder` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Chapter 2 — the outcome of the death claim, for` `a Basic Plan part in force since 2020` `and` (`an adult's death claim, part` `in force` `, account value` 100_000_000 `, crime by the Policyholder` TRUE) EQUALS `only the account value under Article 15, of` 100_000_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `9.1 — the payee of` `the account value under Article 15`

